WEBVTT

00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:13,470
Being on a hormone blockers, is there any blood work or other tests I should ask my

00:00:13,470 --> 00:00:16,110
ecology for to keep an eye on?

00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:20,030
No, not really.

00:00:20,030 --> 00:00:25,030
If you want to know your hormone level, the best test to do is the Dutch test, D-U-T-C-H,

00:00:25,030 --> 00:00:30,430
and you can order that through loop of labs, but you really don't need to run it because

00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:34,710
you're if you're on hormone blockers, you're bad estrogen, all your estrogen is going to

00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:36,110
be in the cellar.

00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:41,940
So there's no need to spend the money on that test.

00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,540
Who would run that test?

00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:50,180
Somebody who just followed out they have cancer or, and their doctor wants to put them

00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:54,780
on hormone blockers, and they don't want to go on it, they want to look at their hormone

00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:55,780
levels.

00:00:55,780 --> 00:01:04,340
I just ran a test for somebody and just went over with them two days ago and her bad estrogen,

00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:12,400
her 400-oxy esterone, was elevated, not good, even though her E1, E2, E3, those are your

00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:18,980
standard estergins, were actually the low normal for some reason, most likely a cytokrome

00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:27,500
P450 pathway was pushing it to be converted to the bad estrogen, which can drive cancers

00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,500
hormone-related cancers.

